# =============================================================================
# dc_synth_paper_core.tcl - Design Compiler synthesis of the ON-DIE digital core
#                           of the Huang-2024 split-sampling 16-bit 5-MS/s SAR ADC.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived from dc_synth_v4.tcl by changing exactly four things:
#   1. DESIGN      sar_adc_digital_top -> sar_digi_paper_core
#   2. SV_FILES    sar_reconstruction.sv is DROPPED (the core does not instantiate
#                  it; analysing an unused file would only add elaboration time)
#   3. the SDC     sar_adc_digital_top.sdc -> sar_digi_paper_core.sdc
#   4. the summary text
# Everything else - the guards, the unmapped-netlist check, the clock guard, the
# wire-load note, set_max_area / optimize_netlist -area - is carried over
# DELIBERATELY and byte-for-byte, so that the area of this core and the area of
# the integrated top are comparable line for line.  That comparability is the
# entire purpose of running both.
#
# Optimisation knobs already present (do not "add" them again):
#   set_max_area 0                -> area is already an explicit objective
#   compile_ultra -no_autoungroup
#   optimize_netlist -area        -> post-mapping area recovery
# Clock gating is NOT enabled here; it is under test in the area_lab experiments
# on the integrated top and is not a like-for-like change, so it is left off.
# =============================================================================
