# =============================================================================
# 3. Synthesis
# =============================================================================
# --- clock gating (v4.1) ------------------------------------------------------
# The measured power breakdown put 84 % of the estimate in `u_calib_ctrl`, a
# FOREGROUND engine that runs once at power-up (207 k cycles) and then sits in
# S_DONE forever -- while its 800-odd flip-flops keep being clocked. Nothing was
# gating that clock.
#
# This library ships NO integrated clock-gating cell (no ICG / CLKLAN / CLKG /
# *_CG among the 478 macros), so the tool must build one from a latch plus an AND:
#     TLATXL 36.5904 um^2  +  AND2XL 9.9792 um^2  ~= 46.6 um^2 per group
# which is still cheaper than the enable multiplexer it replaces. That is why the
# area usually goes DOWN as well.
#
# `-sequential_cell latch` is not a preference, it is the only sequential element
# available that can hold the enable across the inactive clock phase.
set CG_OK 1
1
if {[catch {
    set_clock_gating_style -sequential_cell latch -minimum_bitwidth 2 \
                           -control_point before -max_fanout 32
} m]} {
    puts "NOTE: set_clock_gating_style rejected ($m); synthesising without gating."
    set CG_OK 0
}

